  "description": "FOSZEV crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P 21 21 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: C120 H105 Dy4 N16 O25 3+,C1 H4 O1,3(N1 O3 1-),4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.545-5.066 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.37-178.92°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(μ4-OH){(S)-HL2}8](NO3)3·MeOH·4H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
